---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy — loam.dev"
  description="Privacy policy for loam.dev: self-hosted fonts, no cookies, cookiefree Matomo analytics. Data flows: Cloudflare access logs and a GitHub API call on every page."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="wrap docs docs--legal" data-testid="privacy-layout">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <h1 class="h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Sections" data-testid="privacy-toc">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#controller" data-testid="privacy-toc-controller">Controller</a></li>
          <li><a href="#hosting-and-infrastructure" data-testid="privacy-toc-hosting-and-infrastructure">Hosting &amp; Infrastructure</a></li>
          <li><a href="#fonts" data-testid="privacy-toc-fonts">Fonts</a></li>
          <li><a href="#github-api-call" data-testid="privacy-toc-github-api-call">GitHub API Call (Star Badge)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cookies-and-tracking" data-testid="privacy-toc-cookies-and-tracking">Cookies &amp; Tracking</a></li>
          <li><a href="#web-analytics-matomo-cookiefree" data-testid="privacy-toc-web-analytics-matomo-cookiefree">Web Analytics (Matomo, cookiefree)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#your-rights" data-testid="privacy-toc-your-rights">Your Rights</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes-to-this-policy" data-testid="privacy-toc-changes-to-this-policy">Changes to This Policy</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-page prose-page--legal">

      <section>
        <h2 id="controller">Controller</h2>
        <p>
          Silvio Lindstedt<br>
          <a href="mailto:silvio-lindstedt@outlook.com" data-testid="privacy-link-email-controller">silvio-lindstedt@outlook.com</a>
        </p>
        <p>No postal address is required here — this is a non-commercial open-source project to which §5 DDG does not apply.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="hosting-and-infrastructure">Hosting &amp; Infrastructure</h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA).
          Cloudflare automatically records standard server access logs (IP address, browser, page requested, timestamp) for every request.
          These logs are processed by Cloudflare in its role as a data processor and are subject to <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="privacy-link-cloudflare">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.
          The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — legitimate interest in operating a secure, functional website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare may transfer data to the United States. Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) are in place.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="fonts">Fonts</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses the typefaces <strong>Bricolage Grotesque</strong> and <strong>Spline Sans Mono</strong> (both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1), served <strong>self-hosted</strong> from this domain via
          the Fontsource packages <code>@fontsource-variable/bricolage-grotesque</code> and <code>@fontsource/spline-sans-mono</code>.
          No request is made to the Google Fonts CDN or any other third-party font service.
          Your IP address is never sent to Google for font loading.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="github-api-call">GitHub API Call (Star Badge)</h2>
        <p>
          Every page (the star badge sits in the site header) makes a <strong>direct client-side fetch</strong> to the public <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/rest" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="privacy-link-github-api">GitHub REST API</a> (<code>api.github.com</code>) to display the current star count for the loam.dev repository.
          This call is made by your browser and transmits your IP address to GitHub (GitHub, Inc., a Microsoft subsidiary, San Francisco, CA, USA —
          a third country under GDPR). <strong>This call occurs on every page of the site.</strong>
          The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — legitimate interest in showing a live community signal.
          Third-country transfer: GitHub processes data in the United States; an adequacy decision exists for EU–US Data Privacy Framework participants.
          GitHub's privacy policy: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="privacy-link-github-privacy">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="cookies-and-tracking">Cookies &amp; Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and integrates <strong>no advertising services</strong>.
          No consent banner is needed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="web-analytics-matomo-cookiefree">Web Analytics (Matomo, cookiefree)</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses the self-hosted, cookiefree web analytics software Matomo
          (endpoint: <strong>matomo.silvio-und-maik.de</strong>) to produce aggregated,
          statistical evaluations of how the site is used. The analysis is data-economical
          and runs entirely first-party on a server operated by the author. On each page
          access, the following technical characteristics are recorded: an <strong>anonymised IP address</strong> (truncated to 2 bytes before storage), <strong>browser type and version</strong>, the <strong>operating system</strong> reported by the browser, the <strong>device type</strong> (desktop, tablet or
          smartphone), the <strong>screen resolution</strong> (via JavaScript), the
          configured <strong>browser language</strong>, the <strong>country of origin and
          region</strong> (geographically derived from the IP address), the <strong>referrer</strong> (the page from which this website was accessed), and
          the <strong>subpages visited</strong> with time spent and time of visit. In
          addition, anonymous technical performance metrics of the page are recorded
          (the <strong>Core Web Vitals</strong>: loading time of the largest content
          element, visual layout stability and response time to interactions); these
          measurements are purely technical and carry no personal reference.
        </p>
        <p>
          No cookies are set and no information is stored on or read from your device;
          because tracking is cookieless and IP-anonymised, no consent — and therefore no
          cookie banner — is required under § 25 TDDDG.
          There is no profiling, no cross-device tracking, and no sharing with
          third parties. The data is used exclusively for aggregated statistics and cannot
          be linked to individuals. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in
          needs-driven development of this website). You may object to this processing at
          any time (Art. 21 GDPR) — tick the opt-out option in the field below.
        </p>
        <div id="matomo-opt-out"></div>
        <script is:inline src="https://matomo.silvio-und-maik.de/index.php?module=CoreAdminHome&action=optOutJS&divId=matomo-opt-out&language=en&showIntro=1"></script>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="your-rights">Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing,
          data portability, and the right to object. To exercise these rights, contact <a href="mailto:silvio-lindstedt@outlook.com" data-testid="privacy-link-email-contact">silvio-lindstedt@outlook.com</a>.
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="changes-to-this-policy">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy is versioned in the public repository at <a href="https://github.com/silvio-l/loam" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="privacy-link-repo">github.com/silvio-l/loam</a>.
          Material changes will be noted in the repository changelog.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

